  "_README": "Identity of every file in vendor/. `node vendor-build.js --check` verifies each\nsha256 against the bytes on disk, so a hand-edited or swapped library fails\nreview instead of shipping.\n\nWHY THIS EXISTS: eleven of these were committed minified blobs with no recorded\nversion, no integrity hash and no reproducible recipe - React and Babel among\nthem. \"Are we exposed to CVE-X in jspdf?\" could not be answered without\nreverse-engineering a minified file, and nothing would have noticed a blob being\nedited by hand.\n\nA null `version` means it could NOT be established from the committed bytes and\nhas deliberately not been guessed. Establish it by diffing against a published\ntarball, then fill it in here. The sha256 pins the bytes either way, so the file\nis still identified - just not yet named.",
